WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.272
On this slide, we are focusing on pass one argument.

00:00:03.272 --> 00:00:08.527
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.527 --> 00:00:14.727
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:14.727 --> 00:00:17.862
Before clicking Run, predict the output.

00:00:17.862 --> 00:00:24.012
Then run the cell, inspect the result, and change one value or condition at a time.

00:00:24.012 --> 00:00:27.352
Rerun it and explain why the output changed.

00:00:27.352 --> 00:00:32.542
The goal is to understand the relationship between input, process, and output.

00:00:32.542 --> 00:00:36.242
Think about where this function would appear in a larger project.

00:00:36.242 --> 00:00:44.327
Cleaning one value, calculating one metric, or validating one record can become a reusable function applied

00:00:44.327 --> 00:00:45.762
across many rows, files, or notebooks.
